This project includes a transformed version of the feature dataset from:
AntoniosMalak/Predicting-Hit-Songs-Using-Repeated-Chorus
https://github.com/AntoniosMalak/Predicting-Hit-Songs-Using-Repeated-Chorus
Commit: 838e76f96f7aa755a882b4d2581afe1e0ad3f8a9
Source file: Devolp/Final Data.csv
Source repository license: Apache License 2.0.
The complete license is retained in licenses/DATASET_APACHE_2_0.txt.

Changes: source audio paths removed, metadata renamed, stable track IDs added.
The source's feature naming and extraction conventions inform chorus_hit/audio.py.
New training, evaluation, demo, tests, and documentation were written for this project.

The conceptual reference is Eric Liu's 2021 CS229 report:
Predicting Hit Songs Using Repeated Chorus.
https://cs229.stanford.edu/proj2021spr/report2/81974051.pdf

The dataset is a separate public reproduction, not Eric Liu's original 554-song dataset.
The labels distinguish the source year-end-hit collection from other sampled weekly
chart entries. They must not be described as verified charted/never-charted labels.
